      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14250658/assets/8f7dead46db0b268a9474ad842d8d6077cc84971895e005a3686ab5b18131b6c.png)\n\nThe graph of a function $y=f(x)$ is given above. Find $a$ such that $f(x)\\to a$ as $x\\to \\infty .$",
      "worked_solution": "On the right of the graph, we see that as $x$ gets larger and larger, the function $f(x)$ levels off to the value of $1.$ We can express this as follows:\n\n$$\nf(x)\\to 1\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to \\infty \n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1.$",
